==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|þorp|lang=non}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|þurpan|lang=sv}}, whence also with German {{term|Dorf}} and Dutch {{term|dorp|lang=nl}}.

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|g=n}}

# {{context|before 16th century}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other settlements
# {{context|16th century}} ''Officially defined'' as a very small farm
# {{context|17th century to early 20th century}} A small farm, [[rent]]ed from a larger [[land owner]], where the rent was payed through work on the owner's land ([[dagsverken]])
# {{context|after the 1940's}} A small [[cottage]] in the [[countryside]]

